# Noma project rules

## Scope

- **Corridor**: Nigeria diaspora → Nigeria only. Do not add other corridors without explicit approval.
- **Chain**: Monad only. No Moove, Arc, Base, or other chain-specific code in this repo.

## Secrets and configuration

- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, or private RPC URLs in source.
- Use `.env` / `.env.local` and document placeholders in `.env.example` only.

## Smart contracts

- Every change under `contracts/src/` requires a matching Foundry test under `contracts/test/`.

## Chain data

- Do not guess chain IDs, RPC URLs, or contract addresses.
- Read from [Monad official docs](https://docs.monad.xyz/) or ask the project owner.
- Mark unverified values with `TODO(verify)` in code and docs.

## UI and design

- Use design tokens from `frontend/src/app/globals.css` only (`--bg`, `--surface`, `--accent`, `--text`, `--text-muted`, `--border`).
- Do not introduce hex colors in components except semantic success/error/warning states.
- Prefer small, focused diffs. Ask before changing more than ~5 files in one task.

## Integrations (Agora, wallets, Aurora)

- Do not silently choose Agora Stablecoin API vs direct AUSD, Aurora Intents, or wallet provider (Mera / Privy / Dynamic).
- State assumptions in code comments, `PROGRESS.md`, or PR description and confirm with the team when uncertain.
